<title>ITALY: Italy's Safilo turnover up 35 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Italy's Safilo turnover up 35 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian spectacles maker Safilo said its turnover grew 35 percent to 560 billion lire in 1996 from 1995, while production investment was estimated at 33 billion lire, a statement said.</p>
<p>Safilo said it produced 10 million items in 1996 compared with 8.3 million in 1995. It said after the acquisition of Smith Sport Optics and Carrera Optyl it was the world leader in ski goggles with 1.5 million sold in 1996.</p>
<p>It also said it expected business to increase substantially in 1997.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
